nits. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1196->147. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048297} :encompassing/weight 1.0}] :topic/id #uuid "4681afbb-a1dd-511c-bbd0-1eabc66634e9" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100872 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100694 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315"}] :question/id #uuid "66ec04a0-2af8-5187-98b2-b06eedd5b0a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4406" :question/problem "Find $CD$, if \n\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\nand \n\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nCD=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048297} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048783}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying Two Matrices When They Are Conformable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050407 :topic/title "Multiplying Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "802f0864-9cf0-558a-a018-182bdf8634b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 14 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097948} {:answer/id #uuid "b691c70f-2540-52ab-8dcd-df9ba3df2032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097949} {:answer/id #uuid "fe65f2af-0005-5919-8f19-ecf1b9c126a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 14 \\\\ 14 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097950} {:answer/id #uuid "1c72920d-772a-500b-9395-f0209f18233d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 14 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097951} {:answ