/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9fed3a53-838e-5362-83b9-fbd6582bdbcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-275548" :question/problem "Find $AB,$ if $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is $3\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $A$ and $1$ row in matrix $B$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{A}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 1 & 1\\cdot (-2) \\\\ 2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot (-2) \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 1 & (-2)\\cdot (-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299688 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050407 :topic/title "Multiplying Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90d5156d-1d4d-58d0-b3db-f06dc3110af2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d5156d-1d4d-58d0-b3db-f06dc3110af2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298182} :answer-field/id #uuid "60ee3141-5ab6-5a49-864a-59e094c19044" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type 