186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1050bc77-12b5-5216-85bc-cb476e852617" :question/math-academy-id "q-318484" :question/problem "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $AB.$\n\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,5=5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-15=5\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-2=-2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,6=-2\\cdot (-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -15 \\\\ -2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299689 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050407 :topic/title "Multiplying Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fcdd0ac-c4d8-5dd7-8ce4-29a07e65c610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/