|  | {{field-5}} | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Here, $P$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix and $Q$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix.  \n\nThere is $1$ column in matrix $P$ and $1$ row in matrix $Q$, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n{P}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{Q}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={PQ}_{3\\times 2}\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0\\cdot (-4) & 0\\cdot 2 \\\\ 3\\cdot (-4) & 3\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-4) & (-1)\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -12 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd" :knowledge-point/title "Multiplying a Column-Vector By a Row-Vector" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050407 :topic/title "Multiplying Matrices"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c534267d-c67a-576d-a7c7-8f05a39d217f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396027} {:answer/id #uuid "17ab5397-bb38-59f6-9330-b062d867cf08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396028} {:answer/id #uuid "bbc3f4eb-2bd2-548e-adb8-c1548530611b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186396029} {:answer/id #uuid "cd31fdfe-ca0b-590b-9300-ed3e228812d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/re